# The ROM. Yours, not ours, and never committed. See LEGAL.md.
*.bin
*.smd
*.gen

# NOT "*.md".
#
# ".md" is also a Mega Drive ROM extension, so blocking it looks right — and it
# was here, with an exception list for the documentation. The exception list was
# immediately incomplete: CONTRIBUTING.md was silently ignored the moment it was
# written, and git said nothing until an add failed.
#
# A rule whose exception list has to track every documentation file will be wrong
# again. Markdown collides with it every time; a .md ROM is rare. The real
# barrier is elsewhere: tools/preparar_publico.py refuses binary extensions and
# anything over 1 MB, and .bin covers the format this project actually needs.

# Everything the build produces. This is where the ROM-derived C lives, which
# is precisely why none of it is committed.
build/

# Generated headers: the ROM identity comes from analysis/rom-baseline.json,
# the build version comes from git. Committing copies would create the silent
# divergence this project spends a lot of effort avoiding.
runtime/rom_baseline.h
runtime/versao.h

# Runtime droppings from a development build.
*.log
*.png
*.wav
tinytoon
tinytoon.exe

__pycache__/
*.pyc
